  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Selvi vs The Commissioner on 17 December, 2024 Author: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan Bench: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan 2024:MHC:4177 BEFORE THE MADURAI BENCH OF MADRAS HIGH COURT DATED: 17.12.2024 CORAM THE HONOURABLE MR.JUSTICE G.K.ILANTHIRAIYAN W.P(MD)No.30389 of 2024 and W.M.P(MD)No.25559 of 2024 Selvi ... Petitioner Vs 1.The Commissioner, Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration, DMS Campus,5th Floor, No.359, Anna Salai, Teynampet, Chennai-06. 2.The Designated Officer, Food Safety Department, Vishwanathapuram, Madurai District. 3.The Inspector of Police, Sellur Police Station, Madurai City, Madurai. ... Respondents PRAYER: Writ Petition filed under Article 226 of Constitution of India, to issue a writ of Certiorarified Mandamus calling for records pertaining to the impuned order passed by the second respondent in Na.Ka.No.1468/A2/2024 U.PA.Thu, datd 24.7.2024 and to quash the same and to direct the respondents to de s the Petitioners shop namely, Ganesh Store situted at No.186, Selvi vs The Commissioner on 17 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/112093880/ 1 Kamatchi Nagar, Vaigai Vadakarai, Thathaneri, Madurai District. https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 1/7 For Petitioner : Mr.P.T.Ramesh Raja For RR 1 and 2 : Mr.D.Gandhiraj Spl. Government Pleader For Respondent-3: M/s.M.Aasha Govt . Advocate(Crl . Side) ORDER This Writ Petition has been filed challenging the order passed by the second rspondent dated 24.7.2024 thereby sealed the premises of the Petitioner 2.3.4 of the Food Safety and Standards Rules, 2006. This was clearly illegal. The Designated Officer does not have the jurisdiction to seal the premises on his own. H o w e v e r , t h e l e a r n e d c o u n s e l f o r t h e P e t i t i o n e r , o n i n s t r u c t i o n s , s t a t e s t h a t https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis",
    "facts": "The second respondent had inspected the Petitioners shop and found banned tobacco products from the Petitioners shop and ordered to seal the shop itself by https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis order dated 27\\4.7.2024.The learned counsel for the Petitioner submitted that the second respondent has no power or authority to seal the premises under Section 34 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, if the designated officer is satisfied that the health risk condition exists with respect to any food business, he may aftera notice served on the food business operator apply to the Commissioner of Food Safety for imposing the prohibition.",
    "arguments": "In support of his contention,the learned counsel for the Petitioner relied on an order made in W.P(MD)No.25556 of 2022, ated 5.1.2023 in the case of Kamalakannan .vs. The Commissioner,Tamil nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration Department, DMS Campus, 5th Floor, No.359, Anna Salai, Teynampet, Chennai-6 and others in which it is held as follows: 6.It can be seen there from t Designated Officer can only serve em prohibition notice on the food business operaor and then apply to the Commissioner of Food Safety, who alone can pass an order for sealing the premises. In this case, the Commissioner has passed such an order on 19.10.2022, but the premises came to be sealed on 17.10.2022 itself. 4.Per contra, the learned Special Government Pleader appearing for the respondents 1 and 2 submitted that Rule 2..1.3(4)(1) of the Food Safety and Standards Rules, 2011 permits the second respodnent to seal the premises on certain situations"
  },
